    # prints at half size with the instructions beside it. A gutter of empty
    # grid columns at least this fraction of the page wide, running the FULL
    # height of the content, separates columns. This is the one whitespace
    # split allowed, and only because a vertical gutter is a far stronger
    # signal than the horizontal gap that broke whitespace splitting: a label
    # nearly always has something spanning its own width (a header, a rule, a
    # barcode), so a gutter never falls inside one. The kept column must clear
