    # solid ink: a solid cell whose pixels switch between ink and paper at
    # least this many times per pixel row. A barcode cell measures 27-45 edges
    # over 9 rows; a grey header banner, which is just as solid, measures 0-3.
    # Without this the DPD banner made the instructions side look as solid as
    # the label and the split was refused.
    "STRIPE_EDGES": "1.5",
    # Inside a drawn border cut lines are found at PIXEL level, not on the
    # grid: a run of dark pixel rows reaching across the border's interior,
    # no taller than this fraction of the page's long side (0.003 is 3 rows
